From fce43517b0717c4bd8f47902df1ecfb401b9cb3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:50:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add settings profiles as data, applied through the
 registry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Without this, flipping a repo's regime means hand-editing gates, rails and
protected paths one at a time, and nothing can tell you which regime a repo is
actually in. Profiles are sparse settings maps: the three presets ship as data,
user profiles are plain YAML files in user scope that shadow the presets and
export/import across machines. Apply writes through the canonical config and
stores no active-profile marker, so the active profile is derived by comparing
resolved state — a hand-tuned repo honestly reads custom, with the nearest
profile and the exact drift instead of a dead end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
